.TH PORT 4 "January 2026" "Substrate Kernel" "Device Drivers Manual"
.SH NAME
port \- I/O port access
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /dev/port
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B port
device provides access to the x86 I/O port address space.
Reading and writing to byte offsets in this device corresponds to
.B in
and
.B out
instructions to the respective I/O ports.
.PP
For example, reading byte 0x60 from
.B /dev/port
reads from I/O port 0x60 (keyboard controller data port).
.PP
This device supports only byte-sized (8-bit) I/O operations.
For word or dword I/O, use the
.BR ioperm (2)
or
.BR iopl (2)
system calls with inline assembly.
.SH SECURITY
Access to
.B /dev/port
requires root privileges.
Arbitrary port I/O can cause hardware damage, system instability,
or security vulnerabilities.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /dev/port
I/O port access (character device, major 1, minor 4).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ioperm (2),
.BR iopl (2),
.BR mem (4),
.BR intro (4)
